en:
Do you even intend to listen to me seriously{f:?|, hm?}
{f:Listen, you, that|That}{f: wasn't funny at all.| wasn't much of a joke.}
{f:Lucky for you I'm a gentleman,|This is a real scoop, you know,}{f: because normally you'd get punched out for that.| so guess it properly.}
{f:You'd have no right|You}{f: to complain if you got slugged| really hurt my feelings}, {f:after a remark like that|saying that}.
{f:Look here|Look}, if I were a nutcase, I wouldn't be sitting in a place like this right now, would I?{p}

...And that's my story.
Now that I've surprised you all, let's have the next person talk.
............Huh?
That's the end?
{f:Ending it like this|Ending it like this} is a bit much, isn't it{f:?|?}
Setting aside that ridiculous story about Kazama being an alien, had Kazama actually told us anything at all{f:?|, I wondered?}
{f:This|This just} isn't going to make an article{f:.|.}{p}I'll have to get him to do something about it{f:.|.}

"Huh?"
Kazama looked genuinely surprised.
But he quickly scoffed at me with contempt.{p}

"☆★·☆·★☆·★☆☆"
Huh?
What was that{f:?|?}
What did you just say, Kazama{f:?|?}
That wasn't Japanese{f:.|.}
But it didn't seem like a foreign language either... {f:He'd spoken some strange language!|He'd spoken some strange language!}{p}

Then he stood by the window and raised his hand toward the sky{f:.|.}
"Comrade found!
A Sunbararian had already infiltrated Earth."{p}

At that moment, something like a signal suddenly flashed in the sky{f:.|.}
That was a flying saucer★
No, that's crazy...
While {f:I|I} stood there stunned, Kazama came up to me again and put his arm around my shoulders.
And he whispered in my ear again.
...This time, in Japanese.{p}

"Well, that's fine.
It's only natural that you can't believe me."
Kazama said it with a broad smile.{p}

"Our eyes have degenerated, you see.
Look..."
Kazama jabbed his fingers into his own eyes and gouged them out.{p}

"We can communicate with each other through ultrasound."
He {f:twitched|was twitching} his ears.
Apparently he could move his ears however he liked{f:.|.}
Th-that's amazing{f:!|!}
{f:With|With} that, no wonder he doesn't need eyes{f:.|.}
"And I can do things like this, too."{p}

"Kazama, what are you doing?"
Suddenly, still in that position, Kazama snapped his fingers.
Something went rumble, rumble, rumble.{p}

Ha ha ha, you figured it out.
I was a yokai all along.
You guessed what I really am so easily that it kind of took the wind out of my sails.{p}

"Kazama, come on, that's going way too far.
Please tell us a serious story."
{f:I|I} found myself saying that to Kazama.{p}

"Give me a break☆
Kazama, do you really want to wreck this project that badly?★"
{f:I|I} yelled before I could stop myself.{p}

"Th-there's no need to get so worked up, {c}{f:|}.
I'm not trying to wreck this project, not one bit.
Now, calm down.{p}

...Sure.
I'm the real thing, after all.
Showing you proof is a piece of cake.{p}

"Actually, {f:I|I} am too..."
Thinking this was going nowhere, {f:I|I} found myself {f:pulling|cracking} an improvised joke like that.
Maybe, deep down, {f:I|I} really did have something in common with Kazama.{p}

"Sorry about that. We had a little internal squabble.
Oh, {c}{f:|}!
Could we have a little word later?
...Now then, who's telling the last story?"
Hold on a minute!
What does he mean, a little word{f:?|?}
...Anyway, that doesn't matter right now{f:.|.}
There are six people here, so unless a seventh shows up, the next story {f:will be|has to be} the last.
I {f:have to|have to} hear the last person's story...{p}

"Kazama, come on, that's going way too far.
Please tell us a serious story."
{f:I|I} found myself saying that to Kazama.{p}

"Our eyes have degenerated, you see.
Look..."
Kazama jabbed his fingers into his own eyes and gouged them out.{p}

"Kazama, what are you doing?"
Suddenly, still in that position, Kazama snapped his fingers.
Something went rumble, rumble, rumble.{p}

"{f:Whoaaaaaa|Eeeeeeek}! It's an earthquake{f:!|!}"
{f:I|I} have to get under a desk, fast!
What on earth is {f:going on|going on}?
It's shaking like crazy{f:!|!}
"It's okay, I'll stop it right away."
He said.{p}

"Looks like the earthquake control device is broken☆
What do I do?!"
Don't give me 'what do I do'{f:☆|☆}
At this rate, this whole area is going to collapse{f:!|!}{p}

Right now, everyone is waiting in the rift between dimensions for the results of our survey of Earth.
Our comrades are scouting out other places we might move to, as well, but it's not going too well.
Still, for now Earth is our top candidate for migration.{p}

It all happened in an instant.
What on earth {f:was|was} that?
And those strange words Kazama spoke just now...?{p}

I can't wait.
It's so exciting.
Well, that's the end of my story.
Next person, take it away."
Ah, just thinking about it is going to drive me crazy{f:.|.}
...Is he really a being from another dimension{f:?|?}{p}

"{c}{f:|}, you lied to me just now, didn't you?
It's too late for regrets.
{c}{f:|}, what do you think this is?"{p}

Kazama took a small piece of metal out of his pocket.
......{f:What|What}? It's just an ordinary school badge{f:.|.}
I wish he wouldn't scare me like that{f:.|.}{p}

A tremendous flash of light engulfed {f:us|us}.
He really was an alien{f:.|.}
What an idiot {f:I|I} {f:am|am}.
...It's too late now{f:, isn't it|, isn't it}...{p}

"Kazama, come on, that's going way too far.
Please tell us a serious story."
{f:I|I} found myself saying that to Kazama.{p}

Going along with this stuff... {f:I|I} really am too nice for my own good{f:...|...}
But a tiny part of me thought maybe, just maybe, so {f:I|I} held out.
"Okay, that's enough. Open your eyes."
He said.{p}

{f:I|I}'m going to become a yokai?
{f:Quit joking around|Don't be ridiculous}.
...But the next full moon is only three days away{f:, I think|, isn't it}.
There's nothing to worry {f:about|about}. I just won't believe a word Kazama says{f:.|.}
...As long as I don't believe it.{p}

"Huh?"
Kazama looked genuinely surprised.
But he soon said with a big smile:{p}
